Wyoming state fair department. 25LSO-0492, 1.1
FISCAL NOTE
This bill creates the Wyoming State Fair Department (Department) consisting of
the existing State Fair Division within the Department of Agriculture (DOA). The
State Fair manager previously appointed by the State Fair Board shall serve as
the temporary director for the Department upon the effective date of the bill. As
soon as reasonably practicable, the State Fair Board shall appoint a director of
the Department. A reorganization plan shall not be required of the director of
the Department.
The State Fair Division within the DOA and associated functions for the State
Fair are transferred to the Department under a Type 1 transfer. All positions,
personnel, appropriations, obligations, property, equipment and authority
associated with the State Fair shall be under the control of the Department. The
validity of rules, regulations, contracts, agreements or other obligations of
agencies or programs transferred shall not be affected or impaired.
The Department shall submit a budget in accordance with W.S. 9-2-1010 through 9-
2-1014.
The 2025-26 budget including the Governor’s supplemental budget recommendation
for the State Fair Division is presented below:
